  <prompt>
    Execute the transferred flagship gate G-R2-C: the assistant-driven document lifecycle — open → pre-seed →
    draft-into-editor → AI edit rounds → save-back with provenance — performed by the operator on spaarkedev1
    IN ONE CONVERSATION, browser-verified. The create leg MUST end with the document OPEN in Compose (never a
    record id the user has to go find). A passing curl or green test does NOT satisfy this gate — it requires a
    live browser run. This gate is BLOCKED until the full core-gated chain lands (draft-into-editor, pending
    redline/undo, the catalog rows, dispatch wiring, catalog deploy, optional-association prompt, push/save).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    QA/operator running an end-to-end browser verification of the SpaarkeAi three-pane Compose workspace on the
    spaarkedev1 environment, using the Claude Code Chrome integration (ui-test skill).
  </role>

  <goal>
    A browser-verified pass of the full assistant-driven chain on spaarkedev1 in one conversation: the operator
    opens/pre-seeds a document, drafts into the editor from chat, runs AI edit rounds (draft-alternative +
    accept/reject with visible provenance), and saves back — with the create leg ending with the document OPEN
    in Compose. Evidence (screenshots + narrative) captured. If any leg fails honestly, the gate FAILS and the
    failure mode is reported.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      This gate transferred verbatim from the r2 core charter (former G-R2-A/B/C table) and is THIS project's
      flagship. Spec Success Criterion 1 + design.md §1.5 define it. The create leg's operator-ratified
      refinement: creation completion chains into the chat→Compose bridge + pre-seed automatically; a run where
      the operator must manually open Compose and look up the new document FAILS the leg.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file path="projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/spec.md" role="spec">Success Criteria §1 (flagship gate) + §6 (inline redline ledger-durable).</file>
      <file path="projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/design.md" role="spec">§1.5 delivered-product synopsis + flagship gate script refinement (create leg ends OPEN in Compose).</file>
      <file path="src/solutions/SpaarkeAi/src/components/conversation/ConversationPane.tsx" role="reference">Assistant pane hosting the conversation the gate runs in.</file>
      <file path="src/client/shared/Spaarke.Compose.Components/src/widgets/ComposeWorkspace.tsx" role="reference">Compose editor surface where the document must end OPEN.</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="016" status="blocked">FR-04 draft-into-editor via compose disposition (core-gated).</dependency>
      <dependency task="033" status="blocked">FR-16 pending track-change materialization from ledger.</dependency>
      <dependency task="042" status="blocked">FR-09 compose-draft-alternative Action + Binding (compose disposition).</dependency>
      <dependency task="046" status="blocked">FR-13 dispatch wiring (PaneEventBus compose_action_request).</dependency>
      <dependency task="047" status="blocked">Deploy catalog rows to Dataverse.</dependency>
      <dependency task="014" status="pending">FR-05 optional parent-association prompt (Tier 2c dialog).</dependency>
      <dependency task="055" status="pending">FR-28 push/save deterministic path (gate dialog + OutcomeCard).</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="spec">Verify by a LIVE browser run on spaarkedev1 in ONE conversation. A passing curl / green test does NOT satisfy the gate.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec">The create leg MUST end with the document OPEN in Compose (chained via the chat→Compose bridge + pre-seed) — a manual lookup FAILS the leg.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-040">Inline redline + undo/replace must be ledger-durable (survive refresh) during the AI edit rounds.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-039">All AI actions dispatch through the shipped session-dispatch seam — zero new endpoints (route audit during the run).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">Fluent v9 + dark-mode surfaces (toolbar, OutcomeCard, Context sections, banner) render correctly in the browser.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <files>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-040-session-ledger.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-039-grounded-execution-closed-catalogs.md</file>
      <file>.claude/adr/ADR-013-ai-architecture.md</file>
      <file>.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md</file>
    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Confirm all dependency legs (016/033/042/046/047/014/055) are ✅ and deployed to spaarkedev1; if any is missing, remain blocked and escalate.</step>
    <step order="2">Deploy the BFF + SpaarkeAi + catalog rows to spaarkedev1; verify build + smoke.</step>
    <step order="3">Run the ui-test browser flow (below) in one conversation; capture screenshots + narrative at each leg.</step>
    <step order="4">Assert the create leg ends with the document OPEN in Compose (no manual lookup); assert redline survives a mid-suggestion refresh.</step>
    <step order="5">Record PASS/FAIL with evidence; on any honest failure, report the failure mode and mark the gate FAILED.</step>
  </steps>

  <ui-tests>
    <ui-test name="open-and-preseed">Operator asks the assistant to open a real document in Compose; verify it mounts under OBO, refresh-surviving (1c path).</ui-test>
    <ui-test name="draft-into-editor">Operator asks "draft an engagement letter into Compose"; verify content materializes in the editor from the stored ledger entry (compose disposition).</ui-test>
    <ui-test name="ai-edit-round-draft-alternative">Operator selects a clause, clicks "Draft alternative"; verify a pending insertion/deletion pair renders with {bindingId}@t{n} provenance and accept/reject controls.</ui-test>
    <ui-test name="redline-refresh-durability">Mid-suggestion, refresh the page; verify the pending redline survives (materialized from the ledger, not a client buffer).</ui-test>
    <ui-test name="undo-replace">Operator says "undo that and try another approach"; verify the prior redline is retracted (ledger supersession) and a fresh proposal applies.</ui-test>
    <ui-test name="provenance-visible">Verify each AI recommendation surfaces clickable sources in the Context pane (audit-only).</ui-test>
    <ui-test name="save-back-and-create-leg">Operator saves; verify the Tier-2c gate dialog (one dialog) + per-step OutcomeCard (container/record/profile/indexing), and that the create leg ends with the document OPEN in Compose — not a bare record id.</ui-test>
    <ui-test name="one-conversation">Verify the entire chain executes within a single conversation (no manual context re-entry).</ui-test>
  </ui-tests>

  <outputs>
    <output type="report">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/notes/flagship-gate-G-R2-C-run.md — screenshots + narrative + PASS/FAIL</output>
    <output type="docs">projects/spaarkeai-compose-r2/tasks/TASK-INDEX.md (status update)</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria testable="true">
    <criterion testable="true">The full chain open → pre-seed → draft-into-editor → AI edit rounds → save-back with provenance runs in ONE conversation on spaarkedev1, browser-verified.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The create leg ends with the document OPEN in Compose (no manual lookup).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Inline redline + undo/replace survive a mid-suggestion refresh (ledger-durable).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every AI recommendation surfaces provenance in the Context pane.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A route audit confirms zero new AI dispatch endpoints were used.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Evidence (screenshots + narrative) is captured; a green test alone is explicitly NOT accepted as satisfying the gate.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>The full core-gated chain is not yet landed + deployed to spaarkedev1: this gate depends on 016 (draft-into-editor), 033 (pending redline), 042 (draft-alternative catalog row), 046 (dispatch wiring), 047 (catalog deploy) — all core-A0-gated — plus 014 + 055. Remain `blocked` until every dependency is ✅ and deployed. Do NOT attempt a partial run; a curl/green test cannot substitute for the live browser verification (spec Success Criterion 1).</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <execution>
    <skill>.claude/skills/task-execute/SKILL.md</skill>
  </execution>
</task>
